{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+, Anti-MRSA", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that this sequence is similar (94.74%) to AOD G=S: 16%, R: 13%, C: 11%. GRAVY: -0.537, mol Wt: 4238.796; mol ex coeff:. Chemical modification: C4-C25 and C11-C33 but C15-C35 disulfide bond can't form due to a mutation of C15 to S15. Activity: weakly active against S. aureus ATCC 43300 or ATCC 25923 or E48 (MIC 64 ug/ml) or greater, S. epidermidis ATCC 12228 or G-81 (MIC 64 ug/ml), E-coli ATCC 25922 (MIC > 64 ug/ml), S- typhimurium CVCC 14028 (MIC> 64 ug/ml), S-flexneri CMCC 51571 (MIC >64 ug/ml), and P-aeruginosa CICC 21625 (M(C> 64 ug/ml).", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "39452871", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Mar Drugs. 2024 Oct 8;22(10):463. doi: 10.3390/md22100463. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP04886", "source_id": "AP04886", "source_numeric_id": "04886", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP04886", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "The Marine Antimicrobial Peptide AOD with Intact Disulfide Bonds Has Remarkable Antibacterial and Anti-Biofilm Activity.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
